  "limitations": "Cutoff 1 is source stage i = 2. The conditional theorem assumes an explicit regular degree-k member C of I and an explicitly selected greatest localized Smith coefficient. The returned product numerator is a compatible integral numerator for the finite selected-coefficient product, but that proxy is not proved primitive, normalized, canonical, unique, or independent of Smith/localization choices and is not identified with Hentzelt's historical R^(2) or a resultant. Later-stage witnesses, the historical R^(i) family, determinant-norm/resultant identification, the parallel R-product half of equation (34), primitive descent, compatible zeros, and multiplicities remain open. NOETH-QA-034 concerns line 13319 outside the target range and does not alter this packaging claim."
